  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Empowerment of the Indigenous People of the M&#xE9;dio Rio Solim&#xF5;es and Afluentes</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CIMI is a service agency of the National Conference of Brazilian Bishops (CNBB) formed in 1972 to provide training, advice and support to indigenous people and organisations, and to promote their rights. CIMI also provides direct services in the field of health, bi-lingual education and legal assistance. CAFOD supports the work of CIMI Tef&#xE9; and two teams that work with the Madih&#xE1; and the Deni indians. CIMI-tefe undertake training and accompaniment to indigenous populations in areas of ethno-development.</narrative>
  </description>
